WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.313
Compliance is usually a
package assembled at the end.

2
00:00:03.313 --> 00:00:05.722
Modernization is the
moment to change that,

3
00:00:05.722 --> 00:00:09.137
because you're choosing the
platform and the pipeline anyway.

4
00:00:09.137 --> 00:00:14.155
A control the platform implements once
is inherited by every application on it,

5
00:00:14.155 --> 00:00:18.412
and a pipeline that keeps its results
writes the evidence as it goes.

6
00:00:18.412 --> 00:00:23.736
Circular A one-thirty also turns legacy
into a compliance question: systems that

7
00:00:23.736 --> 00:00:27.152
can't be protected, including
unsupported software,

8
00:00:27.152 --> 00:00:29.376
get top priority for replacement.

9
00:00:29.376 --> 00:00:33.537
So a retained application on
unsupported software is a finding.

10
00:00:33.537 --> 00:00:37.301
It needs a plan, a risk
acceptance and a review date.

11
00:00:37.301 --> 00:00:39.380
And two officials need to hear early.
